      "content": "but \"some economists and environmentalists\" isn't exactly a strong argument when it's my actual business on the line. and you said the focus wasn't on us, but we're the ones feeling the fallout. if these mandates are essentially just a cost-of-doing-business increase that could force small shops to close, shouldn't they be considered a failure in policy design? it seems like the environmental benefits are being prioritized at the direct expense of the people actually keeping the local economy running. isn't that fundamentally unfair?",
